WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 8.10 · Marketing & Communications
Community building and engagement

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Build a community among your first supporters, connected to the cause and each other, not only to you.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.763
A community is a group of people who feel connected to your cause and to each other, not only to you. Building one early, among your first supporters, widens your reach and tests your ideas.

4
00:00:28.163 --> 00:00:28.763
Ways to build it

5
00:00:28.763 --> 00:00:37.500
Reasons to connect: Events, peer groups, online spaces and shared projects. For example: A monthly baking evening for the stall’s regulars, led by trainees.

6
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:47.719
Roles and recognition: Give people roles, a say and credit, so they co-create with you. For example: Regulars vote for the next seasonal loaf and help run tastings.

7
00:00:47.719 --> 00:00:58.396
Safe spaces: Clear guidelines, respectful moderation and protected personal data. For example: Group rules pinned in the chat, two moderators and phone numbers kept hidden.

8
00:00:58.796 --> 00:00:59.396
Why it matters

9
00:00:59.396 --> 00:01:05.070
1. Your first members tell you what you would not otherwise learn.

10
00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:10.374
2. A community spreads the word further than you can alone.

11
00:01:10.374 --> 00:01:15.567
3. Co-creators stay longer than an audience does.

12
00:01:15.967 --> 00:01:16.567
What it feeds

13
00:01:16.567 --> 00:01:20.759
1. Testing new ideas before you launch them.

14
00:01:20.759 --> 00:01:24.581
2. Finding volunteers and supporters among members.

15
00:01:24.581 --> 00:01:29.033
3. Your measurement: participation and contribution.

16
00:01:29.433 --> 00:01:30.033
What to avoid

17
00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:33.115
Broadcasting more than listening.

18
00:01:33.115 --> 00:01:38.419
Opening spaces you do not have time to look after.

19
00:01:38.419 --> 00:01:42.870
Counting followers instead of participation.

20
00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.270
You design one community you will build from the start.

21
00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:49.270
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:53.870
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
